{"fact_id":"f-qg-0063","specimen":"quantum-gravity","subject_id":"proposed:graviton-string-reinterpretation","predicate":"conceived","value":"1974","when":"1974","source":{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joel_Scherk","title":"Joël Scherk — Wikipedia","type":"encyclopedia","published_or_updated":"2026-06-09"},"retrieved_at":"2026-06-10T02:25:34Z","certainty":0.85,"verification":"pending","agent":"sonnet-harvester-qg-entities-01","notes":"Scherk & Schwarz (and independently Yoneya) 1974: realized string theory necessarily contains a massless spin-2 state = graviton, reinterpreting strings from strong-force models to quantum gravity. Yoneya's paper: 'Connection of Dual Models to Electrodynamics and Gravidynamics', Progress of Theoretical Physics, 1974."}
{"fact_id":"f-qg-0064","specimen":"quantum-gravity","subject_id":"proposed:ashtekar-new-variables","predicate":"formulated","value":"1986","when":"1986","source":{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Loop_quantum_gravity","title":"Loop quantum gravity — Wikipedia","type":"encyclopedia","published_or_updated":"2026-06-09"},"retrieved_at":"2026-06-10T02:25:34Z","certainty":0.85,"verification":"pending","agent":"sonnet-harvester-qg-entities-01","notes":"Ashtekar reformulated GR in Yang-Mills-like language (self-dual connections) in 1986. Paper 'New Hamiltonian formulation of general relativity' published Physical Review D, 1987. Built on Amitabha Sen's 1981 self-dual variables work."}
{"fact_id":"f-qg-0065","specimen":"quantum-gravity","subject_id":"proposed:lqg-discrete-area-spectrum","predicate":"formulated","value":"1994","when":"1994","source":{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Loop_quantum_gravity","title":"Loop quantum gravity — Wikipedia","type":"encyclopedia","published_or_updated":"2026-06-09"},"retrieved_at":"2026-06-10T02:25:34Z","certainty":0.85,"verification":"pending","agent":"sonnet-harvester-qg-entities-01","notes":"Rovelli and Smolin showed area and volume operators have discrete spectra in 1994 (Phys. Rev. D). Wikipedia gives 1994 for this result; specimen says '1994-95'. Spin foams / spin networks revival for LQG: Rovelli-Smolin 1995 (Phys. Rev. D, 'Spin networks and quantum gravity')."}
{"fact_id":"f-qg-0066","specimen":"quantum-gravity","subject_id":"SYMMETRY / group theory (SHARED deep root)","predicate":"formulated","value":"1918","when":"1918","source":{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Noether%27s_theorem","title":"Noether's theorem — Wikipedia","type":"encyclopedia","published_or_updated":"2026-06-09"},"retrieved_at":"2026-06-10T02:25:34Z","certainty":0.8,"verification":"pending","agent":"sonnet-harvester-qg-entities-01","notes":"Emmy Noether's theorem published 1918 ('Invariante Variationsprobleme'). Wikipedia: by March 1918 she had the key ideas; published later that year. Connects symmetry to conservation laws — shared root of both GR (diffeomorphism invariance) and QFT (gauge invariance)."}
{"fact_id":"f-qg-0067","specimen":"quantum-gravity","subject_id":"Riemannian / differential geometry (the math substrate of GR)","predicate":"conceived","value":"1854","when":"1854","source":{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/General_relativity","title":"General relativity — Wikipedia","type":"encyclopedia","published_or_updated":"2026-06-09"},"retrieved_at":"2026-06-10T02:25:34Z","certainty":0.8,"verification":"pending","agent":"sonnet-harvester-qg-entities-01","notes":"Riemann's habilitation lecture 'On the Hypotheses which lie at the Bases of Geometry' 1854 founded Riemannian geometry. Ricci-Levi-Civita tensor calculus published 1900 ('Methodes de calcul differentiel absolu'). Supplied to Einstein by Grossmann ~1912-1913."}
{"fact_id":"f-qg-0068","specimen":"quantum-gravity","subject_id":"proposed:lqg-loop-solutions-jacobson-smolin","predicate":"formulated","value":"1988","when":"1988","source":{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Loop_quantum_gravity","title":"Loop quantum gravity — Wikipedia","type":"encyclopedia","published_or_updated":"2026-06-09"},"retrieved_at":"2026-06-10T02:25:34Z","certainty":0.8,"verification":"pending","agent":"sonnet-harvester-qg-entities-01","notes":"Ted Jacobson and Lee Smolin found loop solutions to the Wheeler-DeWitt equation in Ashtekar variables shortly after 1986. Wikipedia: 'shortly after' Ashtekar's 1986 reformulation. Rovelli joined, leading to the loop representation and LQG. Spin-network revival by Rovelli-Smolin in this period (1988-90 per specimen)."}
{"fact_id":"f-qg-0069","specimen":"quantum-gravity","subject_id":"proposed:gt-hooft-non-renormalizability","predicate":"formulated","value":"1973","when":"1973","source":{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quantum_gravity","title":"Quantum gravity — Wikipedia","type":"encyclopedia","published_or_updated":"2026-06-09"},"retrieved_at":"2026-06-10T02:25:34Z","certainty":0.85,"verification":"pending","agent":"sonnet-harvester-qg-entities-01","notes":"'t Hooft and Veltman proved GR non-renormalizable at one loop with matter, 1973. Goroff-Sagnotti proved pure GR non-renormalizable at two loops: preliminary result 1985 (Physics Letters B 160), full paper 1986 (Nuclear Physics B 266). Per specimen: dormancy trigger."}
